From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maago <maago@example.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 01:33:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Draw both forms, and ask as an API client
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A post's page has two forms, a comment and a file, and its In reads one,
the comment. Since 0029 the page's other form has been drawn by hand:
the file input's name is written in the template, name="file", and when
an attach fails, the page draws again with CommentForm{}, whose textarea
has no name at all. maago gen writes, for each form X, a NewX that
returns the form, empty, each field with its name and label, as a GET
draws it:

    func NewCommentForm() CommentForm
    func NewAttachmentForm() AttachmentForm

- postPage gives the page NewAttachmentForm(), and Attach, drawing the
  page again, NewCommentForm() for the comment form
- post_page.html draws the file field as the comment field is drawn:

      {{with .AttachForm.File}}<label>{{.Label}} <input type="file" name="{{.Name}}"></label>
      {{if .Error}}<p class="error">{{.Error}}</p>{{end}}{{end}}

The permission table asks as an API client too. Every route accepts an
API token, not only the API's; the copied auth makes one for a test,
and maagotest wraps the site with it, as As does with a session:

    token, err := auth.SignInToken(ctx, db, u) // (string, error)
    maagotest.Bearer(h, token)                  // every request: Authorization: Bearer token

- The token is cat's, a third user, neither the author nor staff: the
  role cat_token, after bob and before ann. Its column is bob's, by
  token instead of cookie, and the rows that write make their own
  ("cat의 게시판", "cat의 글", "cat의 API 글"). Not ann's token: ann's
  rows publish, archive and delete her posts, and a second ann would
  find them gone. That an author's token writes as the author is
  TestAPI's, which creates and publishes with ann's token
- TestAPI and TestMe make their token with auth.SignInToken instead of
  NewToken and InsertAPIToken by hand

TestAttachments sees both forms: the page's file field by its label and
name, and after an attach with no file the comment's textarea named
text.

